#
# Conformance case: teleology/notification-wait-task.
#
# A logic:NotificationWaitSchema completes only when a logic:ExternalSignal it
# logic:awaitsSignal (manualSignOff) obtains — the engine learns of completion only by
# being told (manual notification / callback-driven completion). Two gate probes share the
# wait schema but differ in state: at stateReceived the signal has obtained (the engine was
# told → logic:GateAdmitted); at statePending it has not (the wait is pending →
# logic:GateUndetermined carrying a logic:awaitingSignal witness — a judgment withheld, NOT
# a denial, since the signal may still arrive). This is the prescriptive-descriptive
# epistemic boundary made canonical.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in input.nq).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/notification-wait-task/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
